From: "a.tzitanov" <alexypoloz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 16:05:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(search): pre-submit coverage check for answer
 completeness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the agent picks submit_answer, a new coverage_check activity first
judges whether the gathered evidence covers the whole question (all
parts of a multi-part query). If a gap is named, it's fed back into the
reasoning history and one more retrieval round runs instead of
finishing early — the gap-detection plain `agent` mode otherwise lacks
(selfrag gets it from reflective synthesis).

Bounded by max_coverage_checks (default 1) + max_iterations so it
always terminates; fail-open so a flaky check never traps the agent.
Knobs propagated via SearchParams (replay-safe).

Verified against litellm → ollama gemma4:e4b: partial evidence flagged
incomplete with the correct missing part; full evidence passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
